    "module":  "oncology",
    "category":  "disease",
    "description":  "Non-Hodgkin lymphoma (NHL) is a diverse group of blood cancers that includes any lymphoma except Hodgkin lymphoma. NHL arises from B-cells (most commonly), T-cells, or NK-cells at various stages of differentiation. It is the most common haematological malignancy in adults. Presentation varies widely from indolent disease (follicular lymphoma, years of slow progression) to aggressive disease (diffuse large B-cell lymphoma, rapid progression and systemic symptoms). Extranodal involvement (GI tract, CNS, skin, bone marrow) is more common in NHL than HL.",
